          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Russell universes or universes à la Russell are types whose terms are types. In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theories"} type theories
            without a separate type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a term of a Russell universe
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A:U
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HoTT+book"} HoTT book
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rocq"} Rocq
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Agda"} Agda
          %h2#definition_of_a_single_russell_universe Definition of a single Russell universe
          %p
            If the type theory has a separate type judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi U
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash U \; \mathrm{type}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:U}{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}
          %h2#formal_definition_of_a_hierarchy_of_russell_universes Formal definition of a hierarchy of Russell universes
          %p Dependent type theories typically come with a hierarchy of Russell universes, so that all types in the dependent type theory are elements of Russell universes. This is especially the case for dependent type theories without any separate type judgments at all, where types are necessarily defined as terms of Russell universes.
          %h3#without_a_separate_type_judgment Without a separate type judgment
          %p One formal definition of a type theory with a hierarchy of Russell universes is as follows:
          %p
            The type theory has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgments"} judgments
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \; \mathrm{level}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                is a universe level,
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \; \mathrm{prop}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \; \mathrm{true}
                , that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
                proposition,
          %p
            and consists of the formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+%28in+logic%29"} signature
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+arithmetic"} Heyting arithmetic
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peano+arithmetic"} Peano arithmetic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite"} infinite
            number of indices, which are strictly ordered with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+total+order"} strict total order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            and upwardly unbounded, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \lt s(i)
            is true for all indices
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          %p
            Now, we introduce the typing judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a:A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is a term of the type
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %strong Russell universe
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %strong universe à la Russell
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi i
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} level
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mrow
