          %h3#with_a_single_separate_type_judgment With a single separate type judgment
          %p It is also possible to define the hierarchy of Russell universes with a single separate type judgment, such that every single type is in a Russell universe. The advantage of doing so is that one doesn’t need to define the theory of universe levels before defining the type theory; one could instead simply define the natural numbers inside of the type theory itself, along with the hierarchy of Russell universes:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
